+  // A directory named with a trailing separator is still that directory.
+  //
+  // The VFS resolves the path component by component, so a trailing backslash
+  // leaves an empty final component and the lookup misses -- an open of
+  // "\Device\Harddisk0\Partition1\\" fails with X_STATUS_NO_SUCH_FILE even
+  // though the device is mounted and the identical path without the separator
+  // opens fine. XAM's start-up enumerates storage that way and cannot get past
+  // it.
+  //
+  // Normalising here rather than at the call site is deliberate: this entry
+  // point is also reached from inside the kernel implementations themselves,
+  // not only through the __imp__NtCreateFile export, so a guest-side override
+  // never sees those calls.
+  //
+  // The root itself ("\\") keeps its separator; there is no name left if it is
+  // taken away.
+  // 0x5C is a backslash, written numerically so the literal cannot be mangled.
+  while (target_path.size() > 1 && target_path.back() == 0x5C) {
+    target_path.pop_back();
+  }
